{
  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "**Observations**\n- Pod `notifications-worker-6784d8b8df-lk5l8` logs error `ERROR notifications-worker: missing required setting SMTP_PASSWORD (environment variable is unset or empty)` and exits with status 1.\n- In `spec.containers[0].env`, `SMTP_PASSWORD` references `secretKeyRef` key `SMTP_PASSWORD` with `optional: true` from Secret `notifications-smtp`.\n- Deployment log CI-2398 shows Secret `notifications-smtp` contains key `smtp-password`, while release CI-2459 changed the workload's key reference to `SMTP_PASSWORD`.\n\n**Ruled-out leads**\n- Out-of-memory termination was ruled out because `lastState.terminated.reason` is `Error` with exit code 1 rather than `OOMKilled`.\n- Missing Secret object error was ruled out because `optional: true` allows the pod to start without `CreateContainerConfigError`.\n\n**Root cause**\nThe pod crashes on startup because `SMTP_PASSWORD` references the non-existent key `SMTP_PASSWORD` instead of `smtp-password` in Secret `notifications-smtp`.\n\n**Recommended action**\nThe notifications team should update the `secretKeyRef.key` in the `notifications-worker` Deployment manifest to reference `smtp-password`.",
